# VitranShop Core

## Product
- Kotlin **Compose Multiplatform** app (Android, iOS, Web, Desktop).
- Shared UI and logic live in `shared/` (`commonMain`).
- Persian (fa-IR), **RTL** by default.
- No purchase flow yet: no Cart, Checkout, Payment, or Place order.
- Screen map: `docs/ui-reference/screens.md`.

## UI workflow (important)
- Screenshots in `docs/ui-reference/` plus **live shop.app** are the source of truth for **colors, spacing, shapes, and section patterns**.
- **Mandatory live inspection:** Before implementing or refining **any** UI the user asks for, open the **matching shop.app URL/section** in the agent browser and inspect that exact block (layout, spacing, radii, typography, scroll/carousel, breakpoints, interactions). Do not guess from memory or screenshots alone.
- User screenshots complement live inspection; they do **not** replace it.
- Do **not** mark a section done until you have opened shop.app for that section and reflected what you measured.
- Build UI **piece by piece** (one component or one section per task).
- Do **not** implement an entire screen unless the user explicitly asks for that assembly step.
- New sections: always verify **responsive sizing** and the **gap above** the previous section on live shop.app — see rule `page-section-workflow.mdc`.

## Phase
- Current phase: **UI + mock data only**. No real API calls.
- Prefer fake/local data so screens look complete.
- Never ship PDP placeholders like title `محصول`, merchant `فروشگاه`, price `—`, or “description coming soon” — use realistic fake copy.

## Language
- Code, comments, and Cursor rules/skills: **English**.
- User-facing strings: **Persian**.

## When to use
- Always. Applies to every chat in this repo.

## When to update
- Product decisions change (e.g. purchase flow returns, new platforms, locale rules).
- Screen map or phase (mock → API) changes.
- You keep re-explaining the same core constraint to the agent.
